    <string name="routine_massage">Skin care routine</string>
    <string name="desc_massage">A consistent skincare routine helps keep skin healthy, elastic, and protected. Cleanse face morning and evening, apply suitable moisturizer, use daily sunscreen, and gently massage along Langer lines.</string>
    <string name="hydratation">Hydration</string>
    <string name="desc_hydratation">Keeping skin well hydrated helps preserve elasticity, softness, and resilience. Adequate hydration reduces dryness and improves overall skin appearance.</string>
    <string name="protection">Sun protection</string>
    <string name="desc_protection">Protecting skin from UV rays helps prevent premature aging and maintains a healthy look. Daily sunscreen use is one of the most effective skincare practices.</string>
    <string name="lines_massage">Massage along Langer lines</string>
    <string name="lines_massage_desc">Gentle massages along Langer lines can help reduce skin tension and promote even force distribution across the skin.</string>
    <string name="detergency">Cleansing</string>
    <string name="detergency_desc">Daily cleansing removes impurities, excess sebum, and daily residue. Proper cleansing prepares skin for subsequent treatments.</string>
    <string name="eyeliner">Eye contour care</string>
    <string name="eyeliner_desc">The eye contour area is delicate and requires special care. Applying hydrating products from inside out helps maintain elasticity and reduce fatigue.</string>
    <string name="water">Deep hydration</string>
    <string name="water_desc">Deep hydration helps keep skin supple and resilient against daily stress. Regular use strengthens the skin barrier.</string>
    <string name="massage">Forehead massage</string>
    <string name="massage_desc">Gently massaging the forehead with slow movements relaxes facial muscles and reduces daily tension. Follow natural skin direction.</string>
    <string name="optization_skin_care">Skin treatment optimization</string>
    <string name="advice_skin">Skin care and treatment advice</string>
    <string name="meaning_langer">What are Langer lines?</string>
    <string name="description_meaning_langer">Langer lines (skin cleavage or tension lines) are topographical maps indicating the natural orientation of collagen fibers in the dermis.</string>
    <string name="skin_info_dialog_title">Langer lines</string>
    <string name="skin_info_dialog_body">Langer lines follow the direction of collagen fibers in the dermis. Described by Austrian anatomist Karl Langer in 1861, they are essential in surgery: an incision parallel to these lines heals with a less visible scar.</string>
    <string name="skin_info_dialog_close">Got it</string>
    <string name="collagen_dialog_title">Skin collagen</string>
    <string name="collagen_dialog_body">Collagen is the most abundant structural protein in skin, making up 70–80% of dry dermis. Its fibers align along Langer lines, providing mechanical strength and elasticity. Production decreases with age.</string>
    <string name="understand">Got it</string>
